    {
      "id": "06037eebf711e2158a32aad666f6365d6555d6f5",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 906137782,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Bug #16796 is loosely related to this one, I think.  The packet counts are simply too high in some cases.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6624779,
            "username": "cjmaynard",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Christopher Maynard",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6624779/avatar.png?v=1789063434",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/cjmaynard"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-08T13:50:23.678Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-08T14:50:06.513Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 149397749,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-04-10T11:47:04.012Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 6650,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 906252221,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Loosely related, but they do the counting separately so I think it's a case of a similar concept, but not something underlying causes the problem.\n\nAn underlying issue that causes some other issues with Protocol Hierarchy is that the protocol tree doesn't distinguish between the two cases of \"Protocol X comes after protocol Y in the packet\":\n1. \"Protocol X is encapsulated within protocol Y\"\n2. \"Protocol X is a sibling of protocol Y, both encapsulated in protocol Z\"\n\nAnd the protocol hierarchy stats tries to convert into something that does distinguish those two relationships. It does a pretty good job, but X=Y is the tricky case, because there is both:\n\n1. \"Protocol X occurs twice in the packet, as two different sibling PDUs (possibly with other protocols between them carried inside the PDUs)\"\n2. \"Protocol X occurs twice in the packet, because there's an encapsulation like MPLS, L2TP, GRE, or DVB-MPE that e.g. can both contain IP and be contained within it.\"\n\nNot handling 1 leads to #1734, #9032, and others. The fix for those (7f8b3025ef1cde5b80c1e47e14b66a56f2fb9a5e) makes the hierarchy wrong for case 2.\n\n(There can also be problems related to 2 even if the protocol does not appear twice in the same packet; if one packet has PPPOE containing PPP containing IP, but another packet has IP directly, the Protocol Hierarchy can change depending on which packet goes first.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-08T14:50:06.383Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-08T14:50:06.383Z",
